+    /// pushir: hands over the frames held for this client, then pings: its pong
+    /// tells they arrived, and until then they stay held. 64 go at once, then one
+    /// a second; past that, what comes waits (the newest 64) and goes in one
+    /// batch a minute later: a flood wakes a phone once a minute, not each second,
+    /// and the pushes in it come late, not never.
